{
  "_readme": [
    "Gold predicate clusters, hand-labelled over the vocabulary an LLM extractor",
    "ACTUALLY emitted on LoCoMo conversations (123 distinct surface forms from 249",
    "claims, 90 of them singletons). This is not a curated wordlist \u2014 it is the real",
    "output distribution, which is what canonicalization has to survive.",
    "",
    "Labelling rule: two predicates share a cluster only if a value for one could",
    "REPLACE a value for the other without changing what is being claimed. Where a",
    "judgement call was genuinely ambiguous the predicates were left in separate",
    "singleton clusters rather than guessed, so recall here is a lower bound and",
    "precision is not inflated by charitable labelling.",
    "",
    "Singleton clusters are load-bearing: they are the trap set. pet vs pet_name,",
    "artwork_created vs artwork_medium vs artwork_subject, volunteer_cause vs",
    "volunteer_location, hobby vs hobby_duration_years, marital_status vs",
    "marriage_duration. Any system that merges those is destroying facts, and the",
    "pairwise metric will catch it."
  ],
